+
+```sh
+git clone --recurse-submodules --branch codex/native-dirplayer-readiness \
+  https://github.com/iExalt/dirplayer-rs.git dirplayer-readiness
+git clone --recurse-submodules --branch codex/native-dirplayer-dirty-preservation-20260918 \
+  https://github.com/iExalt/dirplayer-rs.git dirplayer-dirty-preservation
+```
+
+The original checkout and nested Ruffle must remain dirty and must not be
+described as containing the readiness receipts.
+
+## Verified baseline
+
+The combined baseline records:
+
+- native library: 636 passed, 0 failed;
+- native production-parser integration: 1 passed, 102 filtered;
+- production `wasm-pack build --target web`, including `wasm-opt`: passed;
+- generated-binding TypeScript check: passed;
+- production React/frontend build: passed;
+- combined production browser fixture gate: 22 passed, 0 failed.
+
+The timer receipt separately records 18 manager tests and 38 browser-owner
+lifecycle tests from the same frozen timer source identity. They are reused
+receipts from that source, not a claim that every later source path was rerun.
+
+## Native route and probe result
+
+The probe uses the existing native test harness and one owned session per
+process. `TestHarness::load_movie` reads the local DCR, parses it through
+`read_director_file_bytes`, and mounts it through `load_movie_from_dir_owned`.
+Initialization calls `run_movie_init_owned`. The synthetic fixture proves all
+four authored handlers independently: `prepareMovie`, `startMovie`, `enterFrame`,
+and `exitFrame`.
+
+The final snapshot is 32x32 RGBA with a white `(0,0)` corner, a black `(16,16)`
+center, and 576 opaque black pixels. The earlier all-white probe was superseded:
+its visible-pixel predicate counted the white stage background and did not prove
+authored shape visibility. The final PNG's remaining 448 opaque white pixels are
+inspection evidence, not the acceptance predicate.
+
+The bounded `step_frame` probe does not complete a post-init step. It reaches the
+existing native renderer-binding boundary (`owned player has no renderer`). The
+native timeout host adapter also reports `TimeoutHostDispatch::Unsupported`;
+manual timeout firing in the test harness is not production timer support.
+
+## Explicit limits
+
+- The 47 configured licensed/public movie paths are absent, so the licensed
+  campaign is 47/47 unavailable and was not run.
+- `cargo check --tests --target wasm32-unknown-unknown` remains unresolved with
+  14 configuration-specific `E0599` errors in test-only native helper calls.
+  Production WASM and browser-test WASM paths pass.
+- There is no successful post-init frame step in the native route.
+- This report makes no audio, Flash, Bevy, native Ruffle, Spybot, or native
+  product-readiness claim.
+- Stage 2 ownership completion and Stage 3 independent-session/lifecycle/static
+  proof remain mandatory final gates.
+
+## First bounded implementation item
+
+The next item is an owned native presentation service/policy and a caller-driven
+monotonic frame/timeout pump around the existing `RuntimeSession`, player, owner,
+command-loop, `load_movie`, `init_movie`, and `step_frame` boundaries.
+
+Acceptance should proceed in this order:
+
+1. bind an explicit native presentation policy without browser DOM/canvas
+   assumptions;
+2. drive monotonic frame and timeout advancement from the caller, with stable
+   equal-deadline ordering and teardown;
+3. replay bounded step/per-frame script state and assert the transition;
+4. add one input and then exact RGBA capture.
+
+This is a single-session implementation entry point. It does not waive the final
+Stage 2/3 ownership and isolation gates, and it does not begin audio, Flash,
+Bevy, or Spybot integration.
+
+## Resume commands
+
+Use the isolated worktree and its existing shared target:
+
+```sh
+cd /private/tmp/dirplayer-native-readiness-cumulative-20260918
+git status --short --branch
+git rev-parse HEAD
+git show --stat --oneline 7cd3cc78eef4e5745472e41207690f6ce0874c9c
+git show --stat --oneline fff7dcc3804d857c0bc1b48570399bcea7cee5c8
+git show --stat --oneline 1a99d618df29da6a1bf915aee826a3a8e9dcb7be
+git show --stat --oneline e56266293835198bfeb31158cbbcc11233d0c20f
+```
+
+The bounded probe reproduction is recorded in
+`/private/tmp/dirplayer-native-readiness-cumulative-20260918/docs/checkpoints/native-readiness-20260918/native-probe/README.md`;
+the combined and timer commands are recorded in the sibling receipts under
+`/private/tmp/dirplayer-native-readiness-cumulative-20260918/docs/checkpoints/native-readiness-20260918/`.
+No broad rerun is required to consume this handoff.
