+# Native DirPlayer readiness spike
+
+## Objective
+
+Produce a coherent, reproducible starting point for a **single-session native
+Director player**, preserving the ownership work already completed.
+
+The spike includes bounded stabilization and a disposable native probe. It ends
+with a verified checkpoint and an evidence-backed first implementation task—not
+a completed native backend or full ownership refactor.
+
+This document records the completed bounded work; the deferred items below are
+explicit implementation or acceptance work. The architecture roadmap remains in
+[NATIVE_DIR_PLAYER_PLAN.md](NATIVE_DIR_PLAYER_PLAN.md). The detailed runtime
+checklist used for this handoff is the isolated copy at
+`/private/tmp/dirplayer-native-readiness-cumulative-20260918/docs/NATIVE_DIR_PLAYER_IMPLEMENTATION.md`;
+the original dirty checkout is preserved separately.
+
+## Work checklist
+
+- [x] **Establish the source boundary.** The isolated branch records the
+  cumulative root, accepted 62-file overlay, nested accepted commit, original
+  root/nested diffs, untracked archive, and untouched standalone Ruffle. See the
+  readiness report for exact identities and preservation commands.
+- [x] **Finish the existing timer component.** The owner-bound timer source is
+  `fff7dcc3` with evidence `a4aa876d`; native, manager/lifecycle,
+  production-WASM, and four-case browser checks pass. The 14-error wasm test
+  helper check remains explicitly open. Queued input and palette/font ownership
+  remain deferred.
+- [x] **Consolidate and verify the baseline.** The isolated branch combines the
+  accepted components with the timer and FIFO observation fix at source
+  `7cd3cc78`, evidence `731b0d0a`. Remote publication is outside this spike and
+  the childhood checkout remains uncommitted.
+- [x] **Trace the native execution path.** The probe receipt records local load,
+  D5 parse, four startup handlers, CPU bitmap capture, timeout/frame entry
+  points, native `Unsupported` timer dispatch, and teardown, with browser
+  differences called out.
+- [x] **Run a disposable native probe.** The final probe source is `1a99d618`
+  with evidence `3675f526`: four handlers execute and the 32x32 snapshot has a
+  white corner, black center, and 576 opaque black pixels. The earlier all-white
+  probe from `42c21c82`/`7ec67bcc` is superseded. No post-init frame step passes.
+- [x] **Repair concrete stabilization defects.** The timer source and combined
+  baseline repair the observed safe-boundary/FIFO observation defects. Missing
+  native presentation and pump services remain implementation work; no absent
+  backend was hidden by the probe.
+- [x] **Deliver the checkpoint and implementation handoff.** The readiness
+  report and roadmap identify the first bounded native item, exact receipts,
+  reproduction commands, and all deferred Stage 2/3 and product criteria.
+
+## Probe and interface boundaries
+
+Use the existing native test harness and CPU bitmap entry points. Create a small
+synthetic Director-only fixture using the repository's fixture-generation
+conventions; include observable startup/frame script state and a simple bitmap
+or shape. Exclude Flash, audio, external fonts, nested movies, and Xtras from
+this fixture.
+
+Attempt loading, startup, explicit stepping, RGBA capture, and teardown. Add a
+missing-local-resource case. Bound execution so a stalled scheduler produces a
+useful failure report. Record fixture hashes, commands, source identity, script
+state, image output where available, and exact failure boundaries.
+
+Keep probe code separate from production APIs and retain its source and results
+as reproducible spike evidence. Harness success must be distinguished from
+production readiness, particularly where the harness supplies global adapters,
+manual timing, or host stubs.
+
+No new public native API is implemented during the spike. Complete only the
+browser ABI changes already required by the timer contract, keeping Rust,
+frontend bindings, and browser fixtures synchronized.
+
+## Verification and readiness gate
+
+Run tools through mise, reuse existing build caches, and serialize builds against
+frozen source. Use the established external-sandbox execution path for network
+access and browser checks requiring it.
+
+Required verification:
+
+- Native library suite and relevant native integration tests.
+- WASM compilation, focused timer tests, and the existing combined browser
+  fixture suite.
+- Frontend lifecycle/manager tests, generated-binding TypeScript checks, and
+  production VM/frontend builds.
+- Focused regressions for every stabilization repair.
+- Disposable probe results, including explicit failures where native services
+  are absent.
+
+Record source and artifact identities together. Missing licensed movie fixtures
+remain documented coverage gaps; do not silently count them as passing. The full
+ownership scanner may remain non-green and does not block this checkpoint.
+
+**Ready means:** the consolidated baseline passes its required checks; no
+partially integrated component remains in that baseline; unfinished work is
+preserved; and every observed native-path obstacle is classified as either a
+repaired defect or a concrete native implementation task. A probe blocked by an
+identified missing backend is an acceptable discovery result.
+
+## Handoff and stopping rules
+
+Produce a readiness report containing the verified baseline identity,
+reproduction commands, execution-path dependency map, remaining limitations, and
+an ordered native implementation backlog.
+
+Revise the roadmap to permit a bounded single-session native slice while Stage
+2/3 remain final ownership and isolation gates.
+
+The first implementation task qualifies an owned native presentation service and
+policy plus a caller-driven monotonic frame/timeout pump around the existing
+session/player command loop. Replay the bounded step and per-frame state first;
+input and RGBA capture follow after that seam is accepted. Its handoff must name
+the production entry points, required host substitutions, and observable
+acceptance results established by this spike.
+Audio, native Ruffle, Bevy, and Spybot gameplay follow separately.
+
+The selected stopping rule was bounded stabilization plus native-path discovery.
+The timer batch and baseline regressions are recorded above; larger architectural
+dependencies remain explicit implementation work rather than "polish."
